The decision is TRIM at conviction 3, down from HOLD at 4 on 2026-11-08. The stock still looks cheap and the thesis holds, but the scorecard came to 7. A holding needs 8 to keep conviction 4, so this downgrade cuts the position toward the 5% conviction-3 size. CI is about 6.8% of the portfolio now, by my rough count from `state.json`. I logged the change as a `method_change`, because the 2026-11-08 verdict came before the scorecard existed.

I didn't check whether `portfolio.py` actually sizes the trim as expected. I set `entry_price` to null because valuation already scores near its top, so a lower price wouldn't get the stock to conviction 4. That means the daily price watch won't flag CI for a re-buy.
